{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicHierarchy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MetallicHierarchy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.golden_self_similar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.golden_self_similar","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L100-L103","doc":"**Golden self-similarity.** `φ² = φ + 1` — the defining golden identity,\nhere the `n = 1` case of `metallic_sq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_two_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_two_q","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L89-L98","doc":"**Quantum dimension at a metallic ratio.** The Temperley–Lieb loop /\nquantum dimension `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` evaluates to `√(n²+4)` at `q = δ_n`\n(golden → `√5`, silver → `√8 = 2√2`). On the unit circle this scalar is\n`2cos θ ∈ [−2,2]`; here on the real-metallic ladder it is `√(n²+4) ≥ 2`,\nso only `n = 0` (`δ_0 = 1`, value `2`) meets the root-of-unity range — the\nalgebraic reason golden is the *unique* metallic ratio that is also a\nroot-of-unity quantum dimension (`φ = 2cos(π/5)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_sq","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L85-L87","doc":"`δ_n` is a root of `x² − n·x − 1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_one_eq_golden","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_one_eq_golden","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L81-L83","doc":"**Golden is the first rung.** `metallic 1 = φ = (1 + √5)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_inv","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L72-L79","doc":"**Bar-involution pairing.** `(δ_n)⁻¹ = δ_n − n`, i.e. the involution\n`q ↦ q⁻¹` sends the `n`-th metallic ratio to its sub-unit mirror. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_pos","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L68-L70","doc":"`metallic n > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_iff_hecke_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic_iff_hecke_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L43-L66","doc":"**Metallic characterization.** For `q > 0`, the Hecke scalar `q − q⁻¹`\nequals the integer `n` iff `q` is the `n`-th metallic ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sqrt_metallic_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sqrt_metallic_ge","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L38-L41","doc":"`√(n²+4) ≥ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sqrt_metallic_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sqrt_metallic_pos","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L35-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sqrt_sq_metallic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.sqrt_sq_metallic","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L31-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.metallic","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/MetallicHierarchy.lean#L27-L29","doc":"The `n`-th **metallic ratio**: the positive root of `x² − n·x − 1 = 0`.\n`metallic 1 = φ` (golden), `metallic 2 = 1 + √2` (silver), … ","signatureChunk":0}]}